# Vuetify, theme colors, and mobile UI

Use Vuetify components and utility classes first. Use theme tokens from `src/theme/LightTheme.ts`. Custom CSS is a last resort.

## Theme colors

- Bind colors with Vuetify props or token classes: `color="primary"`, `color="error"`, `class="text-primary"`, `bg-surface`, `text-lightText`, `text-darkText`.
- Do not hardcode hex/rgb in templates, scoped CSS, or inline styles when a theme key exists (`primary`, `secondary`, `success`, `error`, `warning`, `info`, `surface`, `background`, `lightprimary`, `borderLight`, etc.).
- New brand colors belong in `LightTheme.ts`, then consumed via props/classes — not one-off CSS.

```vue
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<span style="color: #3e78ff">Label</span>
<div class="my-card">...</div>
<style scoped>
.my-card { background: #fff; padding: 16px; color: #1D2630; }
</style>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<span class="text-primary">Label</span>
<v-card color="surface" class="pa-4 text-darkText">...</v-card>
```

## Prefer Vuetify over custom CSS

- Spacing: `pa-*`, `ma-*`, `ga-*`. Layout: `d-flex`, `align-center`, `justify-space-between`, `flex-column`, `flex-md-row`.
- Type: `text-h6`, `text-body-2`, `text-caption`, `text-medium-emphasis`.
- Display: `d-none`, `d-md-flex`, `d-sm-block`.
- Radius/elevation: `rounded-sm`, `elevation-2`, component props (`rounded="md"`, `variant="tonal"`).
- Grids: `v-row` / `v-col` with `cols`, `sm`, `md`, `lg` — not CSS grid/flex in `<style>` for page layout.
- Add `<style>` only for something Vuetify cannot do (third-party widget, one-off animation). Keep it scoped and still use `rgb(var(--v-theme-primary))` when a color is required.

## Mobile (required)

- Default to `cols="12"`; add `sm` / `md` / `lg` for wider screens.
- Stack on small screens; do not rely on fixed `px` widths, `min-width` that overflows, or hover-only actions.
- Use `order-*` / `order-md-*` when mobile order should differ from desktop.
- Touch targets: buttons/icons at least usable on phone (`size` + padding classes, not tiny custom hit areas).
- Hide/show with breakpoint classes, not JS screen sniffing, unless behavior cannot be expressed with utilities.

```vue
<!-- ❌ BAD: desktop-only row -->
<v-row>
  <v-col cols="4">...</v-col>
  <v-col cols="8">...</v-col>
</v-row>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<v-row>
  <v-col cols="12" md="4">...</v-col>
  <v-col cols="12" md="8">...</v-col>
</v-row>
```
